{"agent":"dx-round-justified","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"Default `require_new_work=True` contradicts the adjacent, still-documented `review.fix_round_free=True` behavior. Concrete failure: an item changes only `src/a.py`; round 1 raises a finding on line 10. The author rewrites line 10 and settles the finding. `fix_round_free` says the next `ddflow review` should run a free delta review of that rewrite. But `require_new_work` sees the reviewed path set is still `{src/a.py}` and there is no untriaged finding, so it skips the reviewer with “nothing new to review” and counts no round. The fix is never reviewed, and this is the default for existing users.","digest":"11f5e97521e3a2b0","location":"ddflow/config_sections/review.py:review.require_new_work","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/config_sections/review.py:review.require_new_work"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"The test is confounded: `_triaged` leaves no untriaged findings and no changed paths, but the immediately preceding `api.review(... full=True)` call on line 79 runs a reviewer and does not triage any new findings that call produces. As a result, the subsequent `_plain` on line 82 is justified by “an untriaged finding”, not necessarily by `[review].require_new_work = false`; a regression where that knob is ignored would still see `out.exit == 0` and `rounds_used == 3`, so the test does not actually exercise the knob it claims to cover.","digest":"6d5e146861e14fbd","location":"tests/test_review_round_justified.py:test_full_and_the_knob_still_run_a_round","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_review_round_justified.py:test_full_and_the_knob_still_run_a_round"}],"chunks_total":3,"coverage":"2/3 chunk(s) reviewed, 1 off-contract","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":12508,"diff_sha":"db88a6374bded40fd2bbf2979bc5554c52813f737afcfa8e78fc54699ae635aa","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,